:"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6bee9de554cb114d732343efbad59ec0783d74c9ddebd84eb42b9ba48c35705e","event_uuid":"7bd57beb-643d-4dbc-a30f-e4a48bad2cd4","position":{"commit_sha":"ff2807321eb88a99d67edd2d83b741878579f967","position":"1788229382253882001-7bd57beb-643d-4dbc-a30f-e4a48bad2cd4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"109696bbb301ef91b874b0f01d3cd4df7f3cc590b71b76a5c08328244e474f1a","event_uuid":"0537c83d-4766-410e-9092-54ebdcae4d47","position":{"commit_sha":"081d5da323215e7e6e90b874abb8d509c840f73b","position":"1788229384997968001-0537c83d-4766-410e-9092-54ebdcae4d47"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA (rebar-debug): CI run 33426859481 Windows job fails twice with `ValueError: the environment variable is longer than 32767 characters` in pytest itself while setting `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST` (`_pytest.runner._update_current_test_var`, log lines 26379-26390 and 26441-26453). The offending node is `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_marker_survives_truncation.py::test_undecorated_text_is_byte_identical_to_the_bare_fitter[far_over_limit-<60000 x chars>]`: the parameter tuple includes the actual 60,000-character string, so pytest’s default param id embeds it in the nodeid and then in `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST`. Local discriminating experiment on macOS constructed that same value and a Windows-cap shim raised the same `ValueError` at length 60171, proving the mechanism without Windows. Legitimacy: defect in the test harness, not product behavior; the scheduled Windows sweep is intended to execute tests, and this case only fails because the test id exposes the payload rather than using the existing short `label`. Attribution: introduced by commit 6724e79e8ff857b54dd36a62006a89445fc10ad6 (`rebar-ticket: 5931-78a3-95d2-44cd`), which added the long `(\"far_over_limit\", \"x\" * 60_000)` parametrization without an explicit short id. Planned repair: make the parameter ids use the short labels so `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST` remains below Windows’ env-var ceiling while leaving the real 60,000-character product input in the test body.","timestamp":1788218332598231748},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction: an earlier Phase 1 RCA comment on this ticket described the separate pytest env-var length failure and belongs to `watertight-sirenian-auk`. The legitimacy checkpoint for THIS ticket is: local runtime simulation with `rebar._store.git_locking.fcntl = None` reproduces `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'flock'` in both `_store_git_op_lock` and `fetch_coordination_lock`, matching CI run 33426859481 (`git_locking.py:224`). But the repository currently states in `scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py:19-20` and commit 5697f2e11179 (`rebar-ticket: 0b31-aeb5-e734-41c9`) that actually using fcntl locking off POSIX is out of scope / Windows is not a declared support target; the prior fix deliberately guaranteed collectability only. Per the reporter’s explicit guard, I am not auto-fixing production locking until that support-scope decision is resolved.","timestamp":1788219053209960886},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA summary: runtime no-fcntl simulation reproduced AttributeError in git_locking._store_git_op_lock and fetch_coordination_lock; fix merged in Gerrit 2468 as 779449bd19fb; close will carry caused_by 9305-b42c-3262-4c58.","timestamp":1788228739078789001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final debug report (rebar-debug):\n- Problem: Windows/no-fcntl runtime paths raised `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'flock'` in git locking.\n- Proven root cause: `git_locking.py` guards `import fcntl` to `None` (`src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py:56-59`) but `_store_git_op_lock` and `_acquire_fetch_coord_flock` called `fcntl.flock` unconditionally (`:224`, `:316`).\n- Proof: local macOS simulation with `git_locking.fcntl = None` reproduced the exact AttributeError before each protected block. After the fix, both `_store_git_op_lock` and `fetch_coordination_lock` enter their protected sections.\n- Defect legitimacy/safety: the affected lock docs say best-effort/unlocked on OS faults (`:205-211`, `:340-344`); `alert_store.py:8-15,55-62` is repo precedent for no-op advisory locking when fcntl is absent.\n- Defect origin: `42076d367e959` (`rebar-ticket: 9305-b42c-3262-4c58`) introduced the unguarded store git-op flock; `aceb6b6a2261` (`ccd2-528c-b4a9-4b90`) copied/extended it for fetch coordination. Closing with `--caused-by=9305-b42c-3262-4c58`, class `plan_defect`; ccd2 is noted as the fetch-sibling origin.\n- Test: `tests/unit/store/test_git_locking_no_fcntl.py` was RED first with the exact AttributeErrors, held out while the fix was written, GREEN after, and a sandboxed defect-seeded mutation (removing the guards) returned it to RED.\n- Fix: when fcntl is None, skip advisory flock acquisition and proceed unlocked; POSIX flock behavior remains covered by existing serialization tests.\n- Validation: targeted relevant suites passed (`tests/unit/store/test_git_locking_no_fcntl.py`, `tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py`: 24 passed); `make lint` passed; `make typecheck` passed; Gerrit 2468 got LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1 and was submitted/merged as 779449bd19fb. A full local `make test` attempt was stopped after a long partial run; cached failure inspection showed an unrelated live Jira ACLI auth failure outside this fix.\n- Scope/caller sweep: `_store_git_op_lock` callers route through `_with_index_lock_retry`/`run_git_write`; `fetch_coordination_lock` callers are `sync._coordinated_fetch` and `git_fetch.fetch_origin`. All retain bounded git/ref-CAS retry as correctness net, so no behavioral dependency blocks the no-op fallback.\n- Siblings: construct sweep of `fcntl.flock` found no additional same git_locking runtime call site beyond the fixed store/fetch locks. Parity rule is \"git advisory lock acquisition must no-op when fcntl is absent\"; library/internal callers route through the fixed core and no separate CLI/MCP surface performs this operation directly. No structural guard added: the existing `check_fcntl_import_guard.py` covers collectability; this runtime behavior is pinned by the regression test.\n- Residual risk/prevention: broader non-git no-fcntl runtime behavior exists in other lock modules but was not part of this git-locking ticket's acceptance criteria; accepted for separate triage only if Windows runtime support is broadened.\n- Replication: the original no-fcntl simulation no longer reproduces after merged commit 779449bd19fb.\n","timestamp":1788228782739860001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788217723482211862,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"51b8ff19-8ced-4162-b89b-7c66d7c5b51e","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"0b31-aeb5-e734-41c9"},{"link_uuid":"7353ab64-ff33-46d4-b11b-7cf23ae93431","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e57c-4b2c-40f8-4652"},{"link_uuid":"0537c83d-4766-410e-9092-54ebdcae4d47","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"9305-b42c-3262-4c58"}],"description":"## Problem\nThe scheduled Test Suite (mirror) Windows sweep reports hundreds of setup errors with `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'flock'`. The suspected path is `src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py`: it explicitly tolerates `import fcntl` failure by setting `fcntl = None`, but later lock acquisition/release call sites invoke `fcntl.flock(...)` unconditionally.\n\n## Plan\n1. Confirm the Windows/no-fcntl contract by inspecting the guarded import, CI sweep matrix, nearby docs/tests, and any existing fallback/no-op/alternative advisory-lock patterns.\n2. Prove the mechanism locally on macOS by simulating Windows with `git_locking.fcntl = None` and driving `_store_git_op_lock` / `fetch_coordination_lock` through tests that fail with the current AttributeError.\n3. If legitimacy is `defect`, preserve Unix behavior exactly and add the smallest no-fcntl-safe branch/fallback consistent with existing precedent.\n4. Add regression coverage for no-fcntl operation and ensure the test has mutation teeth by reintroducing the missing guard in a sandboxed mutation check.\n5. Run targeted tests, then `make lint` and the default suite before Gerrit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A no-fcntl simulation for `_store_git_op_lock` no longer raises `AttributeError` and still executes the protected operation.\n- [x] A no-fcntl simulation for `fetch_coordination_lock` no longer raises `AttributeError` and still preserves existing cleanup semantics.\n- [x] Unix `fcntl.flock` behavior is unchanged and covered by existing tests or a focused assertion.\n- [x] The RCA comment cites the confirmed mechanism, legitimacy source, caller sweep, sibling sweep, and caused-by attribution.\n- [x] Gerrit change is submitted only after `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py","reason":"Potential no-fcntl advisory lock guard if Windows runtime locking is approved as supported."},{"path":"tests","reason":"Potential focused no-fcntl Windows simulation regression tests if repair is approved."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e57c-4b2c-40f8-4652"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7c124966-b91f-4d4e-bc2e-b546ef63f939","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["navapbc/rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","status_fork_resolutions":[{"dropped_uuid":"78c4d405-3700-4b05-af47-6f6c722448fb","winner_uuid":"5c6c0507-8097-4304-89ac-1098810636e5"}],"tags":["ci","windows","debugging"],"ticket_id":"0e7d-ee49-f92b-44c6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep fails when git locking calls fcntl.flock while fcntl is absent","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5c6c0507-8097-4304-89ac-1098810636e5","21994602-914f-4cd8-b833-74c88b9b57dd","7353ab64-ff33-46d4-b11b-7cf23ae93431","6d92d507-18d3-4b9f-a55f-f93d3d07a4df","479731bf-39a3-44d0-b52e-3396a094a468","fbab03a9-b540-4de7-bece-1736fb781857","78c4d405-3700-4b05-af47-6f6c722448fb","ab435715-44da-4b8c-b255-64b9cb821e17","7c124966-b91f-4d4e-bc2e-b546ef63f939","7bd57beb-643d-4dbc-a30f-e4a48bad2cd4","0537c83d-4766-410e-9092-54ebdcae4d47"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788232973506438001,"uuid":"3a00d263-d306-4528-b863-5c670abb20d9"}